===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{place|en|river|cont/Africa}} that rises near [[Johannesburg]] and flows about 1,770 km (1,100 miles) to the [[Indian Ocean]] in [[Mozambique]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1912|author=w:Rudyard Kipling|title=s:The Elephant's Child
|passage=Goodbye. I am going to the great grey-green, greasy '''Limpopo''' River, all set about with fever-trees, to find out what the Crocodile has for dinner.}}
# {{place|en|province|c/South Africa}} which was originally part of {{l|en|Transvaal}}. It was named after the river.

